.TH TTYPE 1
.SH NAME
ttype \- terminal typing practice
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ttype
[OPTIONS] [COMMAND]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Practice prose and code typing in a terminal. Built-in modes include words,
sentences, go, python, sql, shell, regex, backend, and rust.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Start a typing test.
.TP
.B config
Show or change saved defaults.
.TP
.B history
Show recorded test results.
.TP
.B stats
Show aggregate scores.
.TP
.B clear
Delete history, languages, or all saved data.
.TP
.B doctor
Check terminal and data directory support.
.TP
.B update
Check for and install a verified release.
.TP
.B completion
Generate bash, zsh, fish, or PowerShell completion.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --mode MODE
Select words, sentences, sql, go, backend, python, shell, regex, or rust.
.TP
.B --time SECONDS
Run a timed test.
.TP
.B --words COUNT
Run a word-count test.
.TP
.B --blind
Hide typed correctness until word completion.
.TP
.B --zen
Hide the test HUD.
.TP
.B --min-wpm WPM
Fail once a run falls below WPM after the initial grace period.
